"""KeSeV - the KiCad Schematic Viewer, every KiCad version.

KiCad 4/5: "EESchema Schematic File Version 2..4" (.sch); the symbols come
from the legacy libraries ("EESchema-LIBRARY Version 2.x"): the project's
*-cache.lib, the *-rescue.lib and the libraries listed in the .pro file are
found by themselves, others are added with -L.
KiCad 6, 7, 8, 9 and later: the S-expression .kicad_sch, symbols embedded
in the file; project text variables from the .kicad_pro.
The hierarchical sheets are followed in both.

  kesev board.kicad_sch | board.sch [-L extra.lib ...]
  kesev board.kicad_sch --export out.png|out.pdf|out.svg [--sheet N]

Mouse: wheel = zoom, drag (left or middle) = pan, click = select a symbol
(its fields in the panel), double-click a sheet = open it.
Keys: Home/F = fit, Backspace/Alt+Left = parent sheet, Ctrl+F = find,
Ctrl+E = export, Ctrl+P = print, Ctrl+O = open, Ctrl+Q = quit.

Printing: one sheet per paper page, scaled to fit; the pages of the print
dialog are the sheets in the order of the hierarchy tree (1 = root).  All,
the current sheet, a range, or "Selection" = the sheets selected in the tree
(Ctrl/Shift+click).

Units: the scene is in mils, like the files.
"""

